    {
      "text": "Last night, I couldn't fall asleep. My mind was racing. Just one thought after another, no break in between. It started with something small and then somehow 10 minutes later, I'm thinking about where I see myself in five years. It's crazy how fast your brain can jump from something simple to, like, questioning my whole life. I kept tossing around, changed positions a few times, checked the time three times actually and told myself to just stop thinking. But of course, that never works. The more I tried to slow it down, the faster it went. At one point, I just started laughing. I'm lying there in the dark, wide awake, thinking about things that don't even matter. It's like my brain just refuses to shut up sometimes, you know? Eventually I was like, whatever, and just let it happen. I let my thoughts run wild until they kind of started to wear themselves out. And somewhere in the middle of all that noise, I must have drifted off. I guess some nights are just like that. Your body's tired, but your mind still wants to stay up and figure life out at 2:00 in the morning.",
      "start_time": 0.099,
      "end_time": 65.779,
